+# Codex Raw Context Sync Lane Protocol
+
+Status: candidate protocol for `PCKT-ION-CODEX-CARRIER-DOMAIN-CONTROL-PLANE-SETTLEMENT-001`.
+
+## Purpose
+
+The Codex raw context sync lane preserves the practical value of Codex native
+session continuity during ION development without allowing raw model memory,
+chat transcript, or local session state to become ION authority.
+
+ION should not discard raw Codex context. It should quarantine, index, redact,
+and promote it through explicit proof paths.
+
+## Problem
+
+During active development, Codex native rolling context can contain useful
+signals that branch capsules and receipts do not yet capture:
+
+- observed local failure chains
+- tool-call ordering
+- implicit session assumptions
+- partial code archaeology
+- drift symptoms
+- prior debugging hypotheses
+- carrier-specific limitations
+
+Losing that context can slow diagnosis. Treating it as accepted state can corrupt
+ION. The protocol therefore creates a bounded diagnostic lane.
+
+## Lanes
+
+```text
+native Codex session/memory
+  -> local-private raw snapshot
+  -> raw context manifest
+  -> redacted diagnostic excerpt
+  -> rolling context summary
+  -> proof gate / receipt / settlement
+```
+
+## Storage Classes
+
+### 1. Local-private raw snapshot
+
+Allowed only outside committed project state or under an ignored private path.
+Recommended path class:
+
+```text
+.ion_private/codex_raw_context/<agent_tag>/<session_id>/
+```
+
+Required protections:
+
+- gitignored
+- never mirrored to Drive by default
+- never packed into public context packages
+- secret scan before any excerpt
+- optional encryption if the operator enables it
+
+### 2. Raw context manifest
+
+The manifest may live in the branch capsule because it describes the snapshot
+without revealing its contents.
+
+Recommended file:
+
+```text
+ION/05_context/current/agent_context_branches/<branch>/RAW_CONTEXT_MANIFEST.json
+```
+
+Minimum schema:
+
+```json
+{
+  "schema_id": "ion.codex_raw_context_manifest.v1",
+  "session_id": "codex_session_...",
+  "agent_tag": "codex_local_ion_mason",
+  "branch_id": "branch_...",
+  "packet_id": "PCKT-...",
+  "created_at": "2026-05-12T00:00:00Z",
+  "snapshot_storage_class": "local_private_gitignored",
+  "snapshot_content_committed": false,
+  "snapshot_mirrored_externally": false,
+  "snapshot_hash": "sha256:...",
+  "snapshot_size_bytes": 0,
+  "redaction_status": "not_exported",
+  "diagnostic_excerpt_refs": [],
+  "authority": {
+    "accepted_state_authority": false,
+    "production_authority": false,
+    "live_execution_authority": false,
+    "secrets_authority": false
+  }
+}
+```
+
+### 3. Diagnostic excerpt
+
+A diagnostic excerpt is a reviewed, narrow, redacted piece of raw Codex context
+that exists to explain or debug a specific packet issue. It must include:
+
+- packet id
+- reason for extraction
+- redaction statement
+- line/segment provenance if available
+- non-claim that the excerpt is candidate evidence
+- proof gate or settlement target if it is being used in a decision
+
+## Prohibited
+
+- committing raw `~/.codex` memory/session contents
+- uploading raw session data to Drive by default
+- using raw context as receipt substitute
+- treating raw context as branch-capsule accepted state
+- placing secrets, tunnel credentials, browser profiles, or private logs in a
+  context package
+- allowing a diagnostic excerpt to bypass proof gates
+
+## Cockpit Integration
+
+The cockpit should display raw context sync as a guarded lane:
+
+```text
+Raw context available: yes/no
+Snapshot manifest: present/missing
+Raw content committed: true/false
+External mirror: true/false
+Redaction status: none/reviewed/blocked
+Diagnostic excerpts: count + refs
+Promotion status: none/summary/proof/receipt/settlement
+```
+
+The cockpit must visually separate raw context from accepted ION state.
+
+## Settlement Rule
+
+Raw context may explain why a worker acted, but only proof-gated receipts and
+settlement decide what later workers inherit as state.

